            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DUN01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Henry</forename>
                        <surname>Dundas</surname>
                        <addName>first Viscount Melville</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1742-04-28">
                        <placeName>Scotland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1811-05-27"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The code for Henry Dundas, first Viscount Melville, has also been applied to the entry 'Mr Dundas, Secretary of State'  
      on 08.06.1791, which was the appointment of Dundas as home secretary in <persName key="PIT01">William Pitt's</persName> cabinet, in place of 
    <persName key="GRE03">William Grenville</persName>.  See also the 'public events' files.</p>
                        <p>Other entries relate to his impeachment - the last ever of a British minister - for
    corruption while first lord of the Admiralty and his eventual acquittal.
    Godwin recorded his death, 2 days late, on 29th May.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
